Nethack is a game where part of the challenge derives from requiring
attention to detail (including the details of a user interface which
is suboptimal in intentional, carefully-crafted ways).

IOW, I agree with you, but (in the particular case of nethack, not man-
machine interface design in general) see that as a failing on the part
of the user rather than the software.

Do you really want to deprive future generations of the sublime joy
of being killed by failing to watch the status line?

